From: Gigachad Enthusiast <32457258-AreteMaxxing@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:09:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] War log: turn-start snapshot of the human's units, nearby
 foreign cities and relations

As each tracked player's turn begins (CvPlayer::setTurnActive, after healing and production,
before its moves), the war log now writes:
- I: a header with the counts of the lines that follow;
- L: every unit of the player (id, type, plot, health, experience, level, group, transport,
  cargo, fortify turns, moves left, activity, automation, first queued mission, promotions);
- J: every foreign city with one of its land units that can attack within 3 plots: defence,
  visibility, war, defenders, its units within 1 and 3 plots, and the assault forecast for
  each (chance of capture, expected losses), followed by the defenders as L lines;
- O: its relations to every team met (war, open borders, pact, vassal, war plans, weariness).
F lines record cities founded, and when a log begins, every standing city. C lines add the
attacker and defender ids, U lines the new unit's id, experience, level and promotions, and
A unit missions, automations and commands the unit's id, so every combat, unit and order
joins the unit lines. Tracked players are humans, and player WAR_LOG_SEAT - 1 (new define,
0 = none) for headless test games.

The assault forecast's model moves into AI_assaultForecast, which takes the two unit lists;
CvSelectionGroupAI::AI_cityAssaultForecast collects its lists as before and calls it.

Logging only. The new lines read plain getters (no AI cache, no random number). On a 20-turn
continuation of game 3's save (same seed, seat 12 tracked) the harness telemetry is identical
to main's and so is every war-log line main writes; the first snapshot matches the save's
unit dump in type, experience, level and promotions; every new unit and every combat id
joins the unit lines. Tools tests: 146 passed. Release build: 0 errors, 0 warnings.

